{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And afterward they drew near.</b> After he taught the elders, he goes back and teaches the pericope or the halakhah to Israel. The Sages taught: How was the order of the Mishnah? Moses would learn from the mouth of the Gevurah; Aaron entered — Moses recited his chapter to him; Aaron withdrew and sat at Moses' left; his sons entered — Moses recited their chapter to them; they withdrew; Elazar sat at Moses' right and Itamar at Aaron's left; the elders entered — Moses recited their chapter to them; the elders withdrew and sat at the sides; all the people entered — Moses recited their chapter to them. So it was in the hand of all the people once, in the hand of the elders twice, in the hand of Aaron's sons three times, in the hand of Aaron four times, etc. As is found in Eruvin (54a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:38.580833193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}